  "id": "tactile-agnosia",
  "term": "tactile agnosia",
  "definition": "Tactile agnosia is a type of agnosia in which a person cannot identify an object's shape or what it is by touch alone, even though basic sensation such as light touch and position sense remains intact. More broadly, it reflects difficulty understanding the meaning or significance of sensory input that is not caused by a problem in the primary sensory system.",
